cepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4}=1$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand \n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(0+4)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}-4 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5} & =5 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =25 \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =-9,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $(-9,0)$ and $(1,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab17d171-e676-5149-b166-f3896352ab98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab17d171-e676-5149-b166-f3896352ab98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293603} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc8cb07-521d-571d-9a73-6afdaeae616b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba2a468-f5c7-5336-bbfe-b99876e5e714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ba2a468-f5c7-5336-bbfe-b99876e5e714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293118} :answer-field/id #uuid "327dc828-aa54-5b44-b6b0-c8a5d802a3a9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3df91d88-ab0c-5dc9-a9a3-e62be6f33e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3df91d88-ab0c-5dc9-a9a3-e62be6f33e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293181} :answer-field/id #uuid "e336d56b-437a-5b1b-9376-93777169d13e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d79c3c99-5690-5ca3-b32c-ec3fe16a74cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d79c3c99-5690-5ca3-b32c-ec3fe16a74cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293770} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22d5e13-7b8e-592f-b5dc-bb0d54aed31e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0916b8d4-936c-51d6-aa90-898aaf5837e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-278353" :question/problem "From **left to right,** the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand \n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18} & =2 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =1\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =-5,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $(-5,0)$ and $(7,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c32583-0807-50cf-a7d2-93b5221acc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32c32583-0807-50cf-a7d2-93b5221acc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506001} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a36e933-a342-57e4-aa8d-681fff44a1c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506434} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81dbe94e-47a2-526e-87c4-6d9b611cf210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81dbe94e-47a2-526e-87c4-6d9b611cf210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506133} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7e90dbf-04dd-5b01-8f52-5588cf1af79c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f3c96e2-d65d-5a1b-8c2a-ac6c202d36fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :